Pages = {2580-2582},
Month = {AUG 15},
Abstract = {Motivation: BioContainers (biocontainers. pro) is an open-source and
   community-driven framework which provides platform independent
   executable environments for bioinformatics software. BioContainers
   allows labs of all sizes to easily install bioinformatics software,
   maintain multiple versions of the same software and combine tools into
   powerful analysis pipelines. BioContainers is based on popular
   open-source projects Docker and rkt frameworks, that allow software to
   be installed and executed under an isolated and controlled environment.
   Also, it provides infrastructure and basic guidelines to create, manage
   and distribute bioinformatics containers with a special focus on omics
   technologies. These containers can be integrated into more comprehensive
   bioinformatics pipelines and different architectures (local desktop,
   cloud environments or HPC clusters).
   Availability and Implementation: The software is freely available at
   github.com/BioContainers/.},
